  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Human Communication Layer & Inclusion. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 16: Dan North from SCNA 2013 (2013).",
  "Dan North's keynote at SCNA 2013 reframed craftsmanship from rigid rules to human communication and business empathy.",
  "Who inspired Dan North to challenge dogma? Why did he refuse to monetize or certify Behavior-Driven Development? What principles guided Dan North when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "Roll archive footage (YouTube ID: Bp2lAiqGEMk). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "'Deliberate discovery' assumes ignorance is our constraint. Modern AI prompts fail when they assume certainty; humility yields better architectures. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
